  "body": "The nonsensical \"let the collected string be second\" was spotted and\nfixed by @chaals in the W3C fork: https://github.com/w3c/html/pull/115\n\nThe usual style is to \"let\" a variable when introducing it and to \"set\"\nit when updating it, so do that instead. The new structure ought to be\ncloser to how it would actually be implemented, but no less clear.\n",
